# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and holds every credential this
# project uses — there is no second env file.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The VITE_ prefix is the security boundary: Vite inlines VITE_-prefixed values
# into the public browser bundle at BUILD time and leaves everything else on the
# server. Never move a secret above that line.

# --- Browser (public, inlined into the bundle) -----------------------------
# Leave both blank to run in "direct" mode — the Vite dev proxy fetches NSE and
# Yahoo itself. That works for `npm run dev` only; a production build needs
# Supabase. Fill them in (Supabase dashboard → Connect → Framework) to switch
# the app over to reading pre-ingested rows from your own Postgres.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Legacy projects issue an `anon` JWT instead of a publishable key. Either works.
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Server only (scripts/seed.mjs). NEVER add a VITE_ prefix here. ---------
# The seeding script needs a SECRET key, which bypasses RLS — so it must never
# reach the browser. Dashboard → Project Settings → API keys → secret.
# The seeder reuses VITE_SUPABASE_URL above for the host.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Upstox (server only). NEVER add a VITE_ prefix here. ------------------
# One credential, and only one: the ANALYTICS TOKEN. Upstox → Apps → My Apps →
# Analytics tab → Generate Token. One year, read-only, one per account, no
# OAuth app to create, no redirect URI, and no static IP to whitelist — which
# matters, because Supabase Edge Functions and Cloudflare Workers have no
# stable outbound IP to whitelist in the first place.
#
# It covers Market Quote, Historical Data, Fundamentals, Market Information and
# the websocket feed. What that buys, and the three places the current Yahoo
# path stays better anyway, is written up in plan.md — the short version is that
# it replaces the /v7 cookie+crumb dance, prices NSE Emerge live (retiring the
# bhavcopy walk-back), and turns the screener.in ROCE scrape from 2.5 days into
# ~90 minutes. It does NOT replace Yahoo `spark`: Upstox has no batch candle
# endpoint, so a whole-universe monthly pass is 5,229 requests against 262.
#
# Blank is a supported state. Every Upstox path must degrade to the Yahoo one,
# so the app runs unchanged without this.
UPSTOX_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# The OAuth-app fields, for the path this project does not take. That token
# expires at 3:30 AM IST every day and the standard flow has no refresh token,
# so every pg_cron schedule would break each morning until someone logged in by
# hand. Only fill these if the Analytics tab is unavailable on the account.
UPSTOX_API_KEY=
UPSTOX_API_SECRET=
UPSTOX_REDIRECT_URI=
